0 A lighting lead reaches a small junction box and splits into two thinner branches ending in lamp heads.
0 Name: ELECTRIC_POWER_FUNCTION_CABLE_HALF-Constraints.ldr
0 Author: J.C. Tchang
0 Unofficial Model
0 // Scene: The broad blue cable makes a shallow wave between a plug and a rectangular middle box. Yellow and brown branches leave the box separately, ending in differently oriented lights.
0 // Rigid construction: The rigid pieces are a 58124c02 connector, a 62501c01 light middle box, and horizontal- and vertical-cable light-head variants 62498c02 and 62498c01.
0 // Build lesson: Use real junction and lamp parts to make work lights, inspection lights or a machine headlight pair; leave space for both cable exits.
0 // Reuse: This is a lamp assembly laid out for inspection. Design clips or sockets for the light heads and a secure mount for the middle box in the final model.
0 ROTATION CENTER 0 0 0 1 "Custom" 
0 ROTATION CONFIG 0 0
